From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Alvarado <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:17:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sample: the Gumbel noise's uniform never reaches 1.0

unit() built u as (float)(h >> 40) + 0.5f: for h >> 40 = 2^24 - 1 the sum rounds to
2^24 in float, so u = 1.0 exactly, -logf(-logf(u)) = +inf and that token wins the
Gumbel-max whatever its logit. One value in 2^24 for each of the 129,280 vocabulary
entries: a uniformly random token in ~0.77% of sampled steps (temperature > 0), seen as
stray CJK / Arabic / Hebrew characters and unrelated words in long answers at
temperature 1.0, top-p 1.0. Greedy decoding never reaches this path.

23 bits keep u in [2^-24, 1 - 2^-24], exact in float: the noise stays in [-2.81, 16.64].
---
 ds41f-4xgx10-switchless/engine/model/sample.cu | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ds41f-4xgx10-switchless/engine/model/sample.cu b/ds41f-4xgx10-switchless/engine/model/sample.cu
index 0195aaf..3ac7fc1 100644
--- a/ds41f-4xgx10-switchless/engine/model/sample.cu
+++ b/ds41f-4xgx10-switchless/engine/model/sample.cu
@@ -53,7 +53,10 @@ __device__ __forceinline__ uint64_t mix64(uint64_t x) {
   x ^= x >> 32;
   return x;
 }
-__device__ __forceinline__ float unit(uint64_t h) { return ((float)(h >> 40) + 0.5f) * (1.0f / 16777216.0f); }
+// A uniform in (0, 1), never 0 or 1. 23 bits: with 24, (2^24 - 1) + 0.5f rounds to 2^24 in float, so u was
+// exactly 1.0 once in 2^24, -logf(-logf(1)) = +inf, and that token won whatever its logit: with 129,280
+// vocabulary entries, a uniformly random token in ~0.77% of sampled steps (temperature > 0).
+__device__ __forceinline__ float unit(uint64_t h) { return ((float)(h >> 41) + 0.5f) * (1.0f / 8388608.0f); }
 
 __device__ __forceinline__ bool better(float a, int ia, float b, int ib) { return a > b || (a == b && ia < ib); }
 
